---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site } from '../lib/site';
---

<Base
  title="Petit Planet Release Date, Pre-Download and Platforms"
  description="Petit Planet launches globally on December 4, 2026 on PC, iOS and Android. Pre-download opens December 1. What is confirmed, what is not, and where each fact comes from."
  path="/release/"
>
  <h1>Petit Planet release date and platforms</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    Petit Planet launches worldwide on <strong>December 4, 2026</strong> for PC, iOS and Android. Pre-download opens on
    <strong>December 1</strong>.
  </p>

  <div class="table-scroll">
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr><th>What</th><th>Status</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Global launch</td><td>December 4, 2026</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Pre-download</td><td>From December 1, 2026</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Launch platforms</td><td>PC, iOS, Android, with shared progress across all three</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Nintendo Switch 2</td><td>Announced for 2027, no date yet</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Price</td><td>Free to play</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Server opening time</td><td>Not announced as of {site.updated}</td></tr>
        <tr><td>PlayStation and Xbox</td><td>Nothing announced</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h2>Can I play as soon as I pre-download?</h2>
  <p>
    No. Pre-download only puts the game files on your device ahead of time. Servers open on December 4, and the exact
    hour has not been published yet. This page will be updated when it is.
  </p>

  <h2>Where to pre-register</h2>
  <p>
    Pre-registration is open on the official website, the App Store, Google Play and the Epic Games Store.
    Pre-registering earns the Bestie Star-Light item at launch, and more rewards unlock as global sign-ups pass set
    milestones.
  </p>

  <h2>Will my progress carry between devices?</h2>
  <p>
    Yes for the three launch platforms: PC, iOS and Android share one account and one save. How the Switch 2 version
    will link up has not been explained yet.
  </p>

  <h2>Before launch day</h2>
  <p>
    The <a href="/checklist/">launch checklist</a> puts the practical steps in order, and the
    <a href="/codes/">codes page</a> has the launch code to keep handy.
  </p>

  <p class="small muted">
    Sources: launch date and platforms from
    <a href="https://www.theouterhaven.net/petit-planet-receives-official-release-date/">The Outer Haven</a>;
    pre-download date and pre-registration channels from
    <a href="https://saiganak.com/news/petit-planet-release-date-announcement/">Saiga NAK</a>; Switch 2 timing from the
    <a href="https://gnn.gamer.com.tw/detail.php?sn=314291">official press release as carried by Bahamut GNN</a>;
    pre-registration reward from
    <a href="https://games.gg/petit-planet/guides/how-to-pre-register-for-petit-planet-launch-rewards-guide/">games.gg</a>.
    All checked {site.updated}.
  </p>
</Base>
